thinking:
The issue is clear: `touch_ui_go_back()` hides everything but never shows the main menu again. The fix is to show the main menu after hiding. But there's a subtlety - `touch_ui_show_menu` already handles cleanup (it deletes menu_panel, setting_panel, reminder_panel), so we can just call it. But we need to be careful about the order.

Actually, looking at `touch_ui_show_menu`, it already cleans up all panels:
```c
void touch_ui_show_menu(menu_type_t type)
{
    if (menu_panel) { lv_obj_del(menu_panel); menu_panel = NULL; }
    if (setting_panel) { lv_obj_del(setting_panel); setting_panel = NULL; }
    if (reminder_panel) { lv_obj_del(reminder_panel); reminder_panel = NULL; }
    create_menu_panel(type);
}
```

So the simplest fix is to just replace `touch_ui_go_back()` body with `touch_ui_show_menu(MENU_TYPE_MAIN)`. Let me do that.

